Rule 1 (The reduction dimension dim must be a valid dimension for the input tensor, and the dimension size must be greater than zero.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= -1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1 ∧ shape(v_1, v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (If keepdim is true, the output tensor has dimension size 1 at dim.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : bool} |= if v_3 = true then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if i = v_2 then shape(v_1, i) = 1
>>
Rule 3 (The output should be a tuple of two tensors.)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= v_1.len = 2
